+// (97.5% of the answer tokens). Each row of the result: [draft token, x, 0...] as floats, n_embd wide, so the
+// h_nextn output (llama_get_embeddings_nextn_ith) carries it. A draft is valid only if the sampled token is x.
+// A verify step [t, d] (two tokens, two outputs) runs the head once: on row 1 if the greedy token of row 0 is d (the
+// draft was right, generation goes on from row 1), else on row 0; both result rows hold that one draft.
